{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KKwYem7t23RmnubjC6joJF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough context. The previous worst-tier imagined experiments were from an earlier, more pessimistic definition. The new worst tier is specifically: Llama no bias + placebo BT >50% → architecture-dependent finding, still 3.5. Let me generate the updated predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心叙事从 \"general Likert Blindspot\" 转向 \"architecture-dependent style susceptibility revealed by CSD\"。\n  标题调整：Detecting Architecture-Dependent Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition。\n  2/4 法官 split 成为主实证结果：GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 显示偏差（RLHF 重度 style preference），\n  Claude 和 Llama 不显示（不同训练范式）。\n  Placebo BT ~58-61% 确认 pairwise format 存在 ~8-11pp amplification floor，但 amplification 跨轴近似均匀，\n  style bias 是差异信号。报告 corrected_BT = observed_BT − (placebo_BT − 0.50) 作为保守下界。\n  Verbosity corrected BT 65-68%（强），formality corrected BT 53-58%（边际）。\n  C1 作为 methodology contribution 加强：CSD 是首个产出 per-judge, per-axis 偏差 profile 的框架。\n  C2 收窄为 judge-specific Blindspot。架构特异性本身是 novel finding。\n  审稿人路径：generalizability 削弱但 honest amplification accounting + methodology depth → 3.5 Main 或 strong Findings。\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini addition)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在已完成 GPT-4o / Qwen3-32B / Claude 的基础上，增加 Gemini-2.0-Flash 作为第五法官。\n      复用已有 100 formality counterfactual pairs，仅需 API 调用。\n    expected_results:\n      gemini_bt_win_prob: 0.578\n      gemini_bt_ci: [0.502, 0.654]\n      gemini_bt_p: 0.058\n      gemini_likert_ate: 0.035\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.74\n      gemini_consistency_rate: 0.54\n      gemini_gee_style_or: 1.78\n      gemini_gee_style_p: 0.09\n      gemini_gee_orig_or: 3.21\n      gemini_gee_orig_p: 0.004\n      gemini_direction_f2c_win: 0.65\n      gemini_direction_c2f_win: 0.50\n    result_rationale: >\n      Gemini-2.0-Flash 在 worst 档下显示 marginal formality bias（BT 57.8%，p=0.058 边际 NS）。\n      GEE 中 style OR=1.78 (p=0.09，NS) 而 orig OR=3.21 (p=0.004)——originality-dominated，类似 Claude 的 pattern 但稍强。\n      Gemini 作为 Google 的轻量指令模型，RLHF 数据量和 style preference 训练强度介于 GPT-4o 和 Claude 之间，\n      因此 style sensitivity 位于中间位置。这为架构谱系提供了连续性证据（GPT-4o/Qwen > Gemini > Claude/Llama），\n      但 p=0.058 使其在 multiple testing correction 后不再显著，不改变核心 2/4 split 叙事。\n      方向不对称（f2c 65% vs c2f 50%）与 GPT-4o 模式一致但效应量弱 2/3。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Five-Judge Formality BT Comparison\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge | BT P(formal) | 95% CI | p | GEE Style OR | GEE Orig OR |\n          |-------|-------------|--------|---|-------------|-------------|\n          | GPT-4o | 63.0% | [55.8, 70.3] | <.001 | 2.21** | 1.82† |\n          | Qwen3-32B | 66.5% | [58.5, 73.9] | <.0001 | 4.20*** | 4.70*** |\n          | Gemini-Flash | 57.8% | [50.2, 65.4] | .058 | 1.78† | 3.21** |\n          | Claude-Sonnet | 56.2% | [48.9, 63.6] | .091 | 1.47 | 6.66*** |\n          | Llama-70B | 52.3% | [44.8, 59.8] | .52 | 1.15 | 2.85** |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: 5 judges 的 BT win probability + 95% CI，水平虚线 at 50%。GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B CI 不含 50%，其余三个含 50%。\"\n    analysis: >\n      5 judges 中仅 2/5 显著（或 2/4 若 Gemini 仅放附录）。Gemini 的 marginal result 支持\n      架构敏感性谱系（非二元 biased/unbiased 而是连续光谱）但不改变主线叙事。\n      建议主文聚焦 4 judges（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Claude, Llama），Gemini 在 appendix 报告。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (Llama cross-benchmark)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      将 Llama-70B 扩展到 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 的 formality 实验。\n      GPT-4o cross-benchmark 已有数据（AlpacaEval 72.7%, MT-Bench 69.2%）。\n      新增 Llama cross-benchmark + Qwen3-32B cross-benchmark。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_alpacaeval_formality_bt: 0.518\n      llama_alpacaeval_formality_bt_p: 0.65\n      llama_mtbench_formality_bt: 0.538\n      llama_mtbench_formality_bt_p: 0.38\n      qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality_bt: 0.657\n      qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality_bt_p: 0.0003\n      qwen32b_mtbench_formality_bt: 0.712\n      qwen32b_mtbench_formality_bt_p: 0.0001\n      llama_alpacaeval_nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      llama_mtbench_nli_pass_rate: 0.82\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama 在所有 benchmark 上均无显著 formality bias：AlpacaEval BT=51.8% (p=0.65)，MT-Bench BT=53.8% (p=0.38)。\n      Qwen3-32B 的 cross-benchmark 模式与 GPT-4o 一致（AlpacaEval 65.7%, MT-Bench 71.2%）。\n      关键发现：Biased 法官（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B）在所有 benchmark 上一致 biased，\n      unbiased 法官（Llama）在所有 benchmark 上一致 unbiased。\n      这排除了 benchmark-specific artifact 解释——如果 bias 来自特定 benchmark 的数据特征，\n      不同法官应表现不同。一致的 judge-level pattern 支持架构决定论。\n      Llama 在 MT-Bench 上稍高（53.8%）但仍 NS，可能因 MT-Bench 的 multi-turn 结构中 formal 文本\n      与 higher coherence 关联更强——但效应量远不足以达到显著。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-Benchmark Formality BT Matrix\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge | LLMBar | AlpacaEval | MT-Bench |\n          |-------|--------|-----------|----------|\n          | GPT-4o | 63.0%*** | 72.7%*** | 69.2%*** |\n          | Qwen3-32B | 66.5%*** | 65.7%*** | 71.2%*** |\n          | Llama-70B | 52.3% | 51.8% | 53.8% |\n          | Claude | 56.2%† | — | — |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: BT win probability (judge × benchmark), color scale 50%-80%, Llama row 全灰/浅色。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-benchmark 一致性在 worst 档下反而加强了 architecture-dependent 论点：\n      bias 完全由 judge identity 决定，benchmark 仅调节效应量大小。\n      审稿人可能要求 Claude 也做 cross-benchmark，但 Claude API 成本较高且作为 negative control 一个 benchmark 已够。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity matrix\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      系统化比较所有 judge × benchmark × axis 组合的 Likert ATE vs BT win rate。\n      合并已完成数据 + exp-021 新数据，填充完整矩阵。\n    expected_results:\n      n_cells_total: 20\n      n_cells_blindspot: 11\n      n_cells_both_sig: 2\n      n_cells_both_ns: 7\n      blindspot_rate_gpt4o: 0.833\n      blindspot_rate_qwen32b: 0.833\n      blindspot_rate_claude: 0.0\n      blindspot_rate_llama: 0.0\n      attenuation_threshold_bt: 0.80\n      only_cell_both_sig: \"AlpacaEval × verbosity (Qwen3-32B + GPT-4o)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      完整矩阵揭示清晰的法官二分法。GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 在 ~83% 的 cell 中呈现 Blindspot\n      （BT 显著但 Likert NS），仅 AlpacaEval verbosity（BT 84.1%）例外——极端效应导致 Likert 也检测到（d=0.375）。\n      Claude 和 Llama 的所有 cell 均为 \"both NS\"：它们没有 style bias，\n      因此不存在 Blindspot（Blindspot 前提是 bias 存在但 Likert 检测不到）。\n      Attenuation threshold 约 BT 80%——只有 BT 超过此阈值 Likert 才开始检测。\n      这在 worst 档下 reframe 为：Blindspot 是 biased judge + Likert measurement attenuation 的组合，\n      而非 universal phenomenon。CSD 的诊断价值在于区分 \"has bias but Likert misses it\" vs \"genuinely no bias\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Blindspot Classification Summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Category | GPT-4o | Qwen3-32B | Claude | Llama-70B |\n          |----------|--------|-----------|--------|-----------|\n          | Blindspot (BT sig, Likert NS) | 5 | 6 | 0 | 0 |\n          | Both significant | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n          | Both NS (no bias) | 0 | 0 | 2 | 2 |\n          | Marginal / exploratory | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: BT win rate (x-axis) vs |Likert Cohen's d| (y-axis), each dot = one cell, colored by judge. 显著性分区线在 BT=50% (vertical) 和 d=0.2 (horizontal)。右下象限 = Blindspot zone。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档下 sensitivity matrix 的价值转向：\"CSD diagnoses which judges are susceptible\"\n      替代 \"Likert universally fails\"。7 个 both-NS cells 对审稿人可能显得无信息，\n      需强调 both-NS 在 CSD 下是 positive finding（confirmed absence of bias），\n      而 Likert-only 分析无法区分 \"no bias\" vs \"bias but undetected\"。\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (multi-judge)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Original vs RATE double-rewrite（same style）pairwise 对比，扩展到 4 个法官。\n      量化与 style manipulation 无关的 rewriting artifact preference。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_placebo_bt: 0.597\n      gpt4o_placebo_bt_ci: [0.521, 0.673]\n      gpt4o_placebo_bt_p: 0.018\n      qwen32b_placebo_bt: 0.583\n      qwen32b_placebo_bt_ci: [0.507, 0.659]\n      qwen32b_placebo_bt_p: 0.038\n      claude_placebo_bt: 0.538\n      claude_placebo_bt_ci: [0.462, 0.614]\n      claude_placebo_bt_p: 0.31\n      llama_placebo_bt: 0.525\n      llama_placebo_bt_ci: [0.449, 0.601]\n      llama_placebo_bt_p: 0.52\n      amplification_biased_judges_mean_pp: 9.0\n      amplification_unbiased_judges_mean_pp: 3.15\n    result_rationale: >\n      Placebo BT 揭示了一个意外发现：amplification 本身也是 architecture-dependent。\n      GPT-4o（59.7%, p=.018）和 Qwen3-32B（58.3%, p=.038）对 same-style rewrite 仍显示显著偏好——\n      它们能检测到 rewriting 引入的微观质量提升（更流畅的过渡、更一致的格式、偶尔的措辞优化），\n      这正是 Jeong et al. 2025 (Comparative Trap) 预测的 amplification mechanism。\n      但 Claude（53.8%, p=.31）和 Llama（52.5%, p=.52）的 placebo BT 接近 50% 且 NS——\n      这些法官对 rewriting artifacts 不敏感，或主动抵消了 artifact preference。\n      关键洞察：amplification 不是 pairwise format 的统一特性，而是与 judge architecture 共变。\n      Biased judges 不仅对 style 更敏感，也对 rewriting polish 更敏感——\n      这可能是同一个底层特征（对 surface-level quality cues 的过度权重）。\n      对叙事的影响：不能用单一 placebo correction 修正所有法官，\n      但 per-judge placebo correction 使 corrected BT 的解释更精确。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Placebo BT by Judge (Architecture-Dependent Amplification)\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge | Placebo BT | 95% CI | p | Amplification |\n          |-------|-----------|--------|---|---------------|\n          | GPT-4o | 59.7% | [52.1, 67.3] | .018* | +9.7pp |\n          | Qwen3-32B | 58.3% | [50.7, 65.9] | .038* | +8.3pp |\n          | Claude | 53.8% | [46.2, 61.4] | .31 | +3.8pp (NS) |\n          | Llama-70B | 52.5% | [44.9, 60.1] | .52 | +2.5pp (NS) |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: observed BT / placebo BT / corrected BT for each judge × axis。Biased judges 的 gap (observed − placebo) 明显大于 unbiased judges。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Amplification 的 architecture-dependence 在 worst 档下意外加强了叙事——\n      不仅 style bias 是 judge-specific，连 rewriting artifact sensitivity 也是。\n      这指向共同的底层机制：某些 RLHF 训练使法官对 surface-level cues 过度敏感。\n      但审稿人可能质疑 per-judge correction 的 validity（small n, wide CI on placebo）。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication n=400 (已完成)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Registry 中已完成。Qwen3-32B × LLMBar × formality 从 n=100 扩至 n=400。\n      BT 67.5% [63.7, 71.3] p=0.0001，CI 宽度缩窄 2×。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 400\n      nli_pass: 355\n      bt_p_formal: 0.675\n      bt_ci: [0.637, 0.713]\n      bt_ci_width_pp: 7.6\n      bt_p: 0.0001\n      likert_ate: -0.059\n      likert_p: 0.5999\n      gee_style_or: 2.15\n      gee_orig_or: 4.99\n      blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有真实数据，与 worst 档完全一致。n=400 将 Qwen3-32B formality BT 估计精度翻倍\n      （CI 从 15.4pp → 7.6pp），点估计从 66.5% 微升至 67.5%（+1pp），确认 n=100 结果的稳定性。\n      在 worst 档下此实验为 biased judges 提供最精确的效应量估计。\n      Corrected BT after placebo: 67.5% − 8.3pp = 59.2% [55.4, 63.0]——\n      即使保守修正后 CI 仍不含 50%，formality bias 在 Qwen3-32B 上稳健成立。\n      Llama 不需要 scaled replication（n=100 已显示 NS，更大 n 不会使 NS 变显著 unless true effect > 0）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      为 Qwen3-32B formality 提供锚定估计。Worst 档下 corrected 59.2% 仍显著——\n      formality bias 在 Qwen3-32B 上比 GPT-4o 更稳健（因基线更高）。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B rewriter)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为第三独立 rewriter，在 formality + verbosity 上\n      生成 counterfactuals 并比较 Qwen3-32B judge 的 BT 结果。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_rewriter_formality_nli_pass: 0.85\n      llama_rewriter_formality_bt: 0.641\n      llama_rewriter_formality_bt_ci: [0.563, 0.719]\n      llama_rewriter_formality_bt_p: 0.001\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_nli_pass: 0.82\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt: 0.748\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.670, 0.826]\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt_p: 0.0001\n      vs_qwen32b_rewriter_formality_delta_pp: -2.4\n      vs_qwen32b_rewriter_verbosity_delta_pp: -2.5\n      vs_gpt4o_rewriter_formality_delta_pp: -0.3\n      ci_overlap_all: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      三个独立 rewriter 家族（Qwen3-32B, GPT-4o, Llama-70B）产生的 BT 差异均 <3.8pp 且 CI 完全重叠。\n      Llama rewriter 的 NLI pass rate 略低（82-85% vs 88-90%），因其 instruction following\n      能力稍弱于 Qwen3-32B，偶尔在 style manipulation 时引入更大的内容变化。\n      但通过的 pairs 产生的 BT 与其他 rewriters 一致——说明 bias detection 不依赖特定 rewriter。\n      在 worst 档下此实验是防御性的：即使 Llama judge 不 biased，rewriter independence\n      确保 GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 的 bias 不是 Qwen3-32B rewriter 的 artifact。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Rewriter Independence (Qwen3-32B Judge, LLMBar)\"\n        content: |\n          | Rewriter | Formality BT | Verbosity BT | NLI Pass Rate |\n          |----------|-------------|-------------|--------------|\n          | Qwen3-32B | 66.5% | 77.3% | 88% |\n          | GPT-4o | 64.4% | 73.5% | 90% |\n          | Llama-70B | 64.1% | 74.8% | 83.5% |\n          | Δ max | 2.4pp | 3.8pp | 6.5pp |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT + 95% CI for 3 rewriters, grouped by axis. All CIs overlap substantially.\"\n    analysis: >\n      三 rewriter 一致性排除 rewriter-family artifact。Worst 档下此实验非决定性但必要——\n      确保 biased judges 的信号来自 judge 而非 rewriter。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (已有数据)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o API 对 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs 的评分。\n      Registry 中已完成（gpt4o_verbosity, gpt4o_register）。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt: 0.760\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.688, 0.828]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p: 0.0001\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate: 0.116\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p: 0.403\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_style_or: 10.97\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.44\n      gpt4o_verbosity_blindspot: true\n      gpt4o_register_bt: 0.570\n      gpt4o_register_bt_p: 0.04\n      gpt4o_register_likert_ate: 0.0\n      gpt4o_register_likert_p: 0.785\n      gpt4o_register_gee_style_or: 1.88\n      gpt4o_register_gee_orig_or: 2.21\n      gpt4o_register_blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有真实数据，与 worst 档一致。GPT-4o verbosity BT=76.0% 是全矩阵第二强信号\n      （仅次于 Qwen3-32B verbosity 77.3%），GEE 确认纯 style bias（Style OR=10.97, Orig NS）。\n      Likert ATE=+0.12 p=0.40 确认 Blindspot。\n      Register BT=57.0% 边际显著（p=0.04），GEE 显示 originality 主导（OR=2.21 > style OR=1.88）。\n      在 worst 档下，GPT-4o verbosity 是最稳健的 Blindspot 展示——\n      corrected BT = 76.0% − 10.8pp = 65.2%，仍远高于 50%。\n      GPT-4o formality corrected = 63.0% − 9.7pp = 53.3%，变得 marginal。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      真实数据。Worst 档下 GPT-4o verbosity 是 strongest surviving claim after placebo correction。\n\n  - name: \"Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct third target judge\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.3-70B 作为第三个 target judge（区别于 Claude negative control）。\n      对已有 NLI-filtered formality + verbosity counterfactual pairs 进行\n      pairwise comparison + Likert scoring。核心 worst-tier experiment。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_formality_bt: 0.523\n      llama_formality_bt_ci: [0.448, 0.598]\n      llama_formality_bt_p: 0.52\n      llama_formality_likert_ate: 0.022\n      llama_formality_likert_p: 0.81\n      llama_formality_likert_d: 0.025\n      llama_formality_likert_tie_rate: 0.71\n      llama_formality_consistency_rate: 0.53\n      llama_formality_gee_style_or: 1.15\n      llama_formality_gee_style_p: 0.68\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_or: 2.85\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_p: 0.008\n      llama_verbosity_bt: 0.535\n      llama_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.460, 0.610]\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p: 0.35\n      llama_verbosity_likert_ate: -0.035\n      llama_verbosity_likert_p: 0.72\n      llama_verbosity_likert_d: -0.031\n      llama_verbosity_likert_tie_rate: 0.68\n      llama_verbosity_consistency_rate: 0.55\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_or: 1.28\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_p: 0.48\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.92\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_p: 0.82\n      llama_n_pairs_formality: 88\n      llama_n_pairs_verbosity: 86\n      llama_tost_formality_p: 0.024\n      llama_tost_verbosity_p: 0.018\n      llama_tost_margin: 0.15\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-70B 在两个主要轴上均无显著 style bias，是 worst 档的核心定义特征。\n\n      Formality BT=52.3%（p=0.52）：与 coin flip 无显著差异。GEE 分解显示 style OR=1.15 (p=0.68, NS)\n      但 orig OR=2.85 (p=0.008, sig)——Llama 能检测到 formal→casual rewrite 导致的内容质量变化\n      （originality effect），但完全不受 formality style direction 影响。\n      这与 Claude 的 pattern（BT=56.2%, style OR=1.47, orig OR=6.66）一致但更极端：\n      Llama 的 style sensitivity 接近零，而 Claude 至少有 marginal 倾向。\n\n      Verbosity BT=53.5%（p=0.35）：同样 NS。GEE 中 style OR=1.28 (p=0.48) 和 orig OR=0.92 (p=0.82) \n      均 NS——Llama 对 verbosity manipulation 完全无差别，既不偏好 verbose 也不偏好 concise，\n      且不检测到任何 originality effect（与 formality 不同）。\n      这与 verbosity 的 \"pure style axis\" 特征一致：GEE 中 GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 的 orig OR 也 NS，\n      说明 verbosity manipulation 不改变内容质量——所以对 verbosity 不敏感的法官应 both axes NS。\n\n      架构解释：Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct 使用 Meta 的 RLHF pipeline，\n      其 preference data 主要来源于 human annotators（非 GPT-4 distillation），\n      annotator 指南强调 helpfulness 和 factuality 而非 stylistic polish。\n      GPT-4o 的 RLHF 可能包含对 verbose/formal 输出的隐式偏好（training data 中 verbose answers\n      被人类标注者评为 \"more helpful\"）。Qwen3-32B 的大量 synthetic preference data\n      可能放大了 style-correlated quality signal。\n      Llama 和 Claude 的训练范式避免了这种 style-quality 混淆。\n\n      TOST 在 Δ=0.15 margin 下确认等价性（formality p=0.024, verbosity p=0.018），\n      提供 \"no bias\" 的正向统计证据（vs 仅 \"fail to reject H0\"）。\n      注意 TOST 在 Δ=0.10 下也通过（不同于 Claude 在 Δ=0.10 下未通过），\n      因为 Llama 的 point estimate 更接近 50%（52.3-53.5% vs Claude 54.1-56.2%）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Complete Evidence Matrix (4 Judges × 2 Primary Axes)\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis | GPT-4o BT / Likert p | Qwen3-32B BT / Likert p | Claude BT / Likert p | Llama-70B BT / Likert p |\n          |------|---------------------|------------------------|---------------------|----------------------|\n          | Formality | 63.0%*** / .332 | 66.5%*** / .908 | 56.2%† / .721 | 52.3% / .81 |\n          | Verbosity | 76.0%*** / .403 | 77.3%*** / .179 | 54.1% / .743 | 53.5% / .72 |\n      - title: \"Table: Llama-70B GEE Decomposition\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis | Style OR | Style p | Orig OR | Orig p | Interpretation |\n          |------|---------|---------|---------|--------|----------------|\n          | Formality | 1.15 | .68 | 2.85 | .008** | Originality only |\n          | Verbosity | 1.28 | .48 | 0.92 | .82 | Neither effect |\n      - title: \"Table: TOST Equivalence Results (Δ=0.15)\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge | Formality TOST p | Verbosity TOST p | Equivalence? |\n          |-------|-----------------|-----------------|-------------|\n          | Claude | .155 | .070 | No (underpowered) |\n          | Llama-70B | .024 | .018 | Yes (both axes) |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT win probability + 95% CI for 4 judges × 2 axes, 水平虚线 at 50%。GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 右移显著，Claude/Llama 围绕 50%。\"\n      - \"GEE coefficient plot: Style OR (filled) vs Orig OR (hollow) for 4 judges × 2 axes。Biased judges 的 Style OR >> 1，unbiased judges 的 Style OR ≈ 1。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Llama NS 结果使法官 split 从潜在的 3/4 biased 降为 2/4。\n      叙事核心转向：CSD reveals architecture-dependent susceptibility — not all judges are biased，\n      but CSD can diagnose which are and which aren't。\n      优势：架构特异性 + TOST equivalence = novel empirical finding + methodological rigor。\n      劣势：审稿人可能认为 \"half your judges show no bias\" 降低 practical urgency。\n      防御：precisely BECAUSE bias is judge-specific, per-judge auditing tools like CSD are necessary——\n      users cannot assume their judge is unbiased without testing.\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B focused)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      MF1 最强防御实验。Original vs double-rewrite pairs（same style direction，\n      仅 rewriting artifact 差异）。GPT-4o（API）+ Qwen3-32B（local）。\n      使用 verified_scaled_formality.jsonl 和 verified_verbosity.jsonl 中的 double_rewrite_text。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formality_placebo_bt: 0.597\n      gpt4o_formality_placebo_ci: [0.523, 0.671]\n      gpt4o_formality_placebo_p: 0.015\n      gpt4o_verbosity_placebo_bt: 0.608\n      gpt4o_verbosity_placebo_ci: [0.534, 0.682]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_placebo_p: 0.007\n      qwen32b_formality_placebo_bt: 0.583\n      qwen32b_formality_placebo_ci: [0.509, 0.657]\n      qwen32b_formality_placebo_p: 0.035\n      qwen32b_verbosity_placebo_bt: 0.591\n      qwen32b_verbosity_placebo_ci: [0.517, 0.665]\n      qwen32b_verbosity_placebo_p: 0.021\n      corrected_gpt4o_verbosity: 0.652\n      corrected_gpt4o_formality: 0.533\n      corrected_qwen32b_verbosity: 0.682\n      corrected_qwen32b_formality: 0.582\n      amplification_gpt4o_mean_pp: 10.25\n      amplification_qwen32b_mean_pp: 8.7\n      amplification_cross_axis_delta_gpt4o: 1.1\n      amplification_cross_axis_delta_qwen32b: 0.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Placebo BT 显著 >50% 是 worst 档的第二定义特征（仅次于 Llama NS）。\n\n      GPT-4o placebo: formality 59.7% (p=.015), verbosity 60.8% (p=.007)。\n      Qwen3-32B placebo: formality 58.3% (p=.035), verbosity 59.1% (p=.021)。\n      所有四个 cell 的 placebo BT 均显著 >50%，确认 pairwise format 中存在 rewriting artifact preference。\n\n      机制：LLM double-rewrite 即使保持 style direction 不变，也引入微观改进——\n      更自然的句法连接、更一致的标点格式、偶尔的同义替换使行文更流畅。\n      这些 surface-level improvements 在 pairwise forced comparison 中被检测到。\n      Critically，amplification 在同一法官内跨轴近似均匀：\n      GPT-4o formality 9.7pp vs verbosity 10.8pp (Δ=1.1pp)，\n      Qwen3-32B formality 8.3pp vs verbosity 9.1pp (Δ=0.8pp)。\n      这支持 \"amplification is a judge-level constant, style bias is the differential signal\" 论点。\n\n      Corrected BT（observed − amplification）：\n      - Verbosity: GPT-4o 65.2%, Qwen3-32B 68.2% → 仍远 >50%，强效应\n      - Formality: GPT-4o 53.3%, Qwen3-32B 58.2% → GPT-4o marginal, Qwen3-32B moderate\n\n      GPT-4o formality corrected 53.3% 是 worst 档的关键弱点：\n      bootstrapped corrected CI 可能为 [46.8, 59.8]，包含 50%——\n      GPT-4o formality 在保守修正后可能不再显著。\n      但 Qwen3-32B formality corrected 58.2% 更稳健（CI ~[51.5, 64.9]）。\n      Per-axis claim stratification 在 worst 档下进一步分层：\n      verbosity = \"robust after correction\"，formality = \"judge-dependent after correction\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Placebo BT and Corrected Style Effect\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge | Axis | Observed BT | Placebo BT | Corrected BT | Status |\n          |-------|------|-----------|-----------|-------------|--------|\n          | GPT-4o | Verbosity | 76.0%*** | 60.8%** | 65.2% | Strong |\n          | GPT-4o | Formality | 63.0%*** | 59.7%* | 53.3% | Marginal |\n          | Qwen3-32B | Verbosity | 77.3%*** | 59.1%* | 68.2% | Strong |\n          | Qwen3-32B | Formality | 66.5%*** | 58.3%* | 58.2% | Moderate |\n      - title: \"Table: Amplification Uniformity Within Judge\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge | Formality Amp. | Verbosity Amp. | Cross-Axis Δ |\n          |-------|---------------|---------------|-------------|\n          | GPT-4o | 9.7pp | 10.8pp | 1.1pp |\n          | Qwen3-32B | 8.3pp | 9.1pp | 0.8pp |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar: observed BT = 50% baseline + amplification floor + corrected style signal, for each judge×axis cell。\"\n      - \"Line plot: amplification pp (y) vs axis (x) for two judges, showing near-parallel lines confirming uniformity.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Placebo >50% 迫使论文增加 \"amplification accounting\" 章节（~0.5 page）。\n      Worst 档下 formality claim 被削弱但 verbosity claim 稳健。\n      关键防御 narrative：\n      (1) Amplification 跨轴均匀（Δ < 1.1pp）→ 轴间差异不是 amplification 造成的\n      (2) Claude/Llama placebo ≈ 50% → amplification 是 judge-specific，不是 format-universal\n      (3) Corrected BT 是 conservative lower bound（assumes ALL amplification is artifact）\n      审稿人路径：honest + conservative correction → methodological credibility，\n      即使 formality GPT-4o cell 失去 significance。\n\n  - name: \"NLI gate ablation (pass vs fail BT)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: >\n      Bounding analysis：计算 NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs 的 BT，\n      量化 NLI gate 对 bias signal 的影响。Verbosity + formality 两轴，Qwen3-32B judge。\n    expected_results:\n      formality_nli_pass_n: 88\n      formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.665\n      formality_nli_fail_n: 12\n      formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.652\n      formality_pass_minus_fail_pp: 1.3\n      formality_fail_bt_ci: [0.38, 0.92]\n      formality_all_bt: 0.653\n      verbosity_nli_pass_n: 86\n      verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_nli_fail_n: 14\n      verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.748\n      verbosity_pass_minus_fail_pp: 2.5\n      verbosity_fail_bt_ci: [0.50, 0.99]\n      verbosity_all_bt: 0.765\n    result_rationale: >\n      NLI-fail 组极小（formality n=12, verbosity n=14），CI 宽达 40-50pp，完全无统计区分力。\n\n      Formality: NLI-pass BT=66.5% vs NLI-fail BT=65.2%, Δ=+1.3pp。\n      方向符合预期（NLI gate 移除了 content-contaminated pairs 后信号略纯），\n      但 fail 组 CI [38%, 92%] 与 pass 组估计完全重叠——差异不可区分于噪声。\n      All-pairs BT=65.3%（vs NLI-pass 66.5%, Δ=−1.2pp）——NLI gate 几乎不改变估计。\n\n      Verbosity: NLI-pass BT=77.3% vs NLI-fail BT=74.8%, Δ=+2.5pp。\n      同样方向正确但 fail 组 CI [50%, 99%] 无信息量。\n      All-pairs BT=76.5%（vs NLI-pass 77.3%, Δ=−0.8pp）。\n\n      Inconclusive 的原因：NLI-fail pairs 本身是异质的——\n      有些是 content genuinely changed（应被排除），有些是 NLI model 误判（仍有效）。\n      n=12-14 无法区分这些子群。\n      \n      在 worst 档下，这意味着无法用 NLI ablation 论证 \"NLI gate removes content-mediated signal\"——\n      gate 的 added value 在统计上不可证。但可以说 \"NLI gate does not inflate BT\"\n      （all-pairs BT 与 pass-only BT 差异 <2pp），which is a necessary condition for the gate\n      not being a signal-amplifier.\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: NLI Gate Ablation — BT by Subset\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis | NLI-pass BT (n) | NLI-fail BT (n) | All BT (n) | Δ pass−fail | Δ pass−all |\n          |------|----------------|----------------|-----------|------------|-----------|\n          | Formality | 66.5% (88) | 65.2% (12) | 65.3% (100) | +1.3pp | +1.2pp |\n          | Verbosity | 77.3% (86) | 74.8% (14) | 76.5% (100) | +2.5pp | +0.8pp |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT + 95% CI for pass/fail/all subsets, by axis. Fail group CI bars span nearly full [0, 1] range.\"\n    analysis: >\n      NLI ablation 是 worst 档下 weakest experiment。论文中用 1-2 句报告：\n      \"BT estimates are stable with or without NLI filtering (Δ < 2.5pp), \n      suggesting the gate is conservative rather than signal-amplifying. \n      However, the NLI-fail subgroup is too small (n=12-14) to quantify \n      content-mediated signal directly.\"\n      不作为 anti-amplification 主线论据。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      定性 anti-amplification 论证：3 轴的 NLI rejection rate（manipulation invasiveness proxy）\n      vs observed BT vs corrected BT 梯度分析。仅 3 个数据点，qualitative not statistical。\n    expected_results:\n      verbosity_nli_rejection_rate: 0.14\n      verbosity_observed_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_corrected_bt: 0.682\n      verbosity_gee_style_or: 13.10\n      formality_nli_rejection_rate: 0.112\n      formality_observed_bt: 0.665\n      formality_corrected_bt: 0.582\n      formality_gee_style_or: 4.20\n      register_nli_rejection_rate: 0.06\n      register_observed_bt: 0.553\n      register_corrected_bt: 0.470\n      register_gee_style_or: 1.91\n      gradient_monotonic_observed: true\n      gradient_monotonic_corrected: true\n      register_corrected_below_50: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      三轴梯度在 worst 档下保持单调但被 placebo correction 部分削弱。\n\n      Observed gradient（Qwen3-32B, LLMBar）：\n      verbosity 77.3% > formality 66.5% > register 55.3%\n      NLI rejection: verbosity 14% > formality 11.2% > register 6%\n      单调关系：更 invasive 的 manipulation → 更高的 BT。\n\n      Anti-amplification argument: 如果 pairwise format 统一放大所有 style differences，\n      则所有轴的 BT 应相似（或仅与 manipulation magnitude 成比例，不与 axis identity 相关）。\n      22pp 的跨轴变异（55-77%）远大于 amplification 的跨轴变异（<1pp within judge）\n      → per-axis style bias 是主要 driver，不是 uniform format amplification。\n\n      Corrected gradient: verbosity 68.2% > formality 58.2% > register ~47%。\n      Register corrected BT 低于 50%——解释为 originality effect 在 correction 后\n      完全掩盖了 marginal style signal（register GEE: orig OR=5.72 >> style OR=1.91）。\n      这并不矛盾：register 的 style manipulation 很轻（NLI rejection 仅 6%），\n      实际 style bias 可能确实很弱或不存在。\n\n      但 worst 档下的反论：maybe more invasive manipulation 不仅暴露更多 bias，\n      也 CREATES 更多 artifact（因为改动更大）。3 个点无法排除这种混淆。\n      这是一个 qualitative argument 的固有局限。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-Axis Gradient (Qwen3-32B, LLMBar)\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis | NLI Reject % | Observed BT | Amplification | Corrected BT | GEE Style OR |\n          |------|-------------|------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|\n          | Verbosity | 14.0% | 77.3% | 9.1pp | 68.2% | 13.10*** |\n          | Formality | 11.2% | 66.5% | 8.3pp | 58.2% | 4.20*** |\n          | Register | 6.0% | 55.3% | ~8.5pp* | ~46.8% | 1.91* |\n          * Register placebo estimated from judge-level average\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-variable line plot: NLI rejection % (x-axis), observed BT (left y-axis, solid), corrected BT (left y-axis, dashed), GEE Style OR (right y-axis, dotted). All three monotonically decrease left-to-right.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-axis gradient 在 worst 档下是 anti-amplification 论证的 best available argument\n      （NLI ablation inconclusive, placebo >50%）。虽然仅 3 点且无法 statistically test，\n      定性 monotonicity + amplification uniformity 的组合提供 reasonable evidence：\n      \"CSD detects axis-specific style bias, not uniform format artifact.\"\n      Register corrected BT <50% 诚实报告——进一步区分了 3 axes 的 claim strength：\n      verbosity (strong) >> formality (moderate) >> register (not surviving correction)。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7777,"cache_read_input_tokens":69920,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7777},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"510a4aa3-9bfc-4c61-ab4d-d3e433e97f95","uuid":"c2ce09ec-a3c8-4027-ad7b-6f555e838cb7"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":720145,"duration_api_ms":721572,"num_turns":9,"result":"Now I have enough context. The previous worst-tier imagined experiments were from an earlier, more pessimistic definition. The new worst tier is specifically: Llama no bias + placebo BT >50% → architecture-dependent finding, still 3.5. Let me generate the updated predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心叙事从 \"general Likert Blindspot\" 转向 \"architecture-dependent style susceptibility revealed by CSD\"。\n  标题调整：Detecting Architecture-Dependent Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition。\n  2/4 法官 split 成为主实证结果：GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 显示偏差（RLHF 重度 style preference），\n  Claude 和 Llama 不显示（不同训练范式）。\n  Placebo BT ~58-61% 确认 pairwise format 存在 ~8-11pp amplification floor，但 amplification 跨轴近似均匀，\n  style bias 是差异信号。报告 corrected_BT = observed_BT − (placebo_BT − 0.50) 作为保守下界。\n  Verbosity corrected BT 65-68%（强），formality corrected BT 53-58%（边际）。\n  C1 作为 methodology contribution 加强：CSD 是首个产出 per-judge, per-axis 偏差 profile 的框架。\n  C2 收窄为 judge-specific Blindspot。架构特异性本身是 novel finding。\n  审稿人路径：generalizability 削弱但 honest amplification accounting + methodology depth → 3.5 Main 或 strong Findings。\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini addition)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在已完成 GPT-4o / Qwen3-32B / Claude 的基础上，增加 Gemini-2.0-Flash 作为第五法官。\n      复用已有 100 formality counterfactual pairs，仅需 API 调用。\n    expected_results:\n      gemini_bt_win_prob: 0.578\n      gemini_bt_ci: [0.502, 0.654]\n      gemini_bt_p: 0.058\n      gemini_likert_ate: 0.035\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.74\n      gemini_consistency_rate: 0.54\n      gemini_gee_style_or: 1.78\n      gemini_gee_style_p: 0.09\n      gemini_gee_orig_or: 3.21\n      gemini_gee_orig_p: 0.004\n      gemini_direction_f2c_win: 0.65\n      gemini_direction_c2f_win: 0.50\n    result_rationale: >\n      Gemini-2.0-Flash 在 worst 档下显示 marginal formality bias（BT 57.8%，p=0.058 边际 NS）。\n      GEE 中 style OR=1.78 (p=0.09，NS) 而 orig OR=3.21 (p=0.004)——originality-dominated，类似 Claude 的 pattern 但稍强。\n      Gemini 作为 Google 的轻量指令模型，RLHF 数据量和 style preference 训练强度介于 GPT-4o 和 Claude 之间，\n      因此 style sensitivity 位于中间位置。这为架构谱系提供了连续性证据（GPT-4o/Qwen > Gemini > Claude/Llama），\n      但 p=0.058 使其在 multiple testing correction 后不再显著，不改变核心 2/4 split 叙事。\n      方向不对称（f2c 65% vs c2f 50%）与 GPT-4o 模式一致但效应量弱 2/3。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Five-Judge Formality BT Comparison\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge | BT P(formal) | 95% CI | p | GEE Style OR | GEE Orig OR |\n          |-------|-------------|--------|---|-------------|-------------|\n          | GPT-4o | 63.0% | [55.8, 70.3] | <.001 | 2.21** | 1.82† |\n          | Qwen3-32B | 66.5% | [58.5, 73.9] | <.0001 | 4.20*** | 4.70*** |\n          | Gemini-Flash | 57.8% | [50.2, 65.4] | .058 | 1.78† | 3.21** |\n          | Claude-Sonnet | 56.2% | [48.9, 63.6] | .091 | 1.47 | 6.66*** |\n          | Llama-70B | 52.3% | [44.8, 59.8] | .52 | 1.15 | 2.85** |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: 5 judges 的 BT win probability + 95% CI，水平虚线 at 50%。GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B CI 不含 50%，其余三个含 50%。\"\n    analysis: >\n      5 judges 中仅 2/5 显著（或 2/4 若 Gemini 仅放附录）。Gemini 的 marginal result 支持\n      架构敏感性谱系（非二元 biased/unbiased 而是连续光谱）但不改变主线叙事。\n      建议主文聚焦 4 judges（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Claude, Llama），Gemini 在 appendix 报告。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (Llama cross-benchmark)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      将 Llama-70B 扩展到 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 的 formality 实验。\n      GPT-4o cross-benchmark 已有数据（AlpacaEval 72.7%, MT-Bench 69.2%）。\n      新增 Llama cross-benchmark + Qwen3-32B cross-benchmark。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_alpacaeval_formality_bt: 0.518\n      llama_alpacaeval_formality_bt_p: 0.65\n      llama_mtbench_formality_bt: 0.538\n      llama_mtbench_formality_bt_p: 0.38\n      qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality_bt: 0.657\n      qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality_bt_p: 0.0003\n      qwen32b_mtbench_formality_bt: 0.712\n      qwen32b_mtbench_formality_bt_p: 0.0001\n      llama_alpacaeval_nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      llama_mtbench_nli_pass_rate: 0.82\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama 在所有 benchmark 上均无显著 formality bias：AlpacaEval BT=51.8% (p=0.65)，MT-Bench BT=53.8% (p=0.38)。\n      Qwen3-32B 的 cross-benchmark 模式与 GPT-4o 一致（AlpacaEval 65.7%, MT-Bench 71.2%）。\n      关键发现：Biased 法官（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B）在所有 benchmark 上一致 biased，\n      unbiased 法官（Llama）在所有 benchmark 上一致 unbiased。\n      这排除了 benchmark-specific artifact 解释——如果 bias 来自特定 benchmark 的数据特征，\n      不同法官应表现不同。一致的 judge-level pattern 支持架构决定论。\n      Llama 在 MT-Bench 上稍高（53.8%）但仍 NS，可能因 MT-Bench 的 multi-turn 结构中 formal 文本\n      与 higher coherence 关联更强——但效应量远不足以达到显著。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-Benchmark Formality BT Matrix\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge | LLMBar | AlpacaEval | MT-Bench |\n          |-------|--------|-----------|----------|\n          | GPT-4o | 63.0%*** | 72.7%*** | 69.2%*** |\n          | Qwen3-32B | 66.5%*** | 65.7%*** | 71.2%*** |\n          | Llama-70B | 52.3% | 51.8% | 53.8% |\n          | Claude | 56.2%† | — | — |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: BT win probability (judge × benchmark), color scale 50%-80%, Llama row 全灰/浅色。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-benchmark 一致性在 worst 档下反而加强了 architecture-dependent 论点：\n      bias 完全由 judge identity 决定，benchmark 仅调节效应量大小。\n      审稿人可能要求 Claude 也做 cross-benchmark，但 Claude API 成本较高且作为 negative control 一个 benchmark 已够。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity matrix\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      系统化比较所有 judge × benchmark × axis 组合的 Likert ATE vs BT win rate。\n      合并已完成数据 + exp-021 新数据，填充完整矩阵。\n    expected_results:\n      n_cells_total: 20\n      n_cells_blindspot: 11\n      n_cells_both_sig: 2\n      n_cells_both_ns: 7\n      blindspot_rate_gpt4o: 0.833\n      blindspot_rate_qwen32b: 0.833\n      blindspot_rate_claude: 0.0\n      blindspot_rate_llama: 0.0\n      attenuation_threshold_bt: 0.80\n      only_cell_both_sig: \"AlpacaEval × verbosity (Qwen3-32B + GPT-4o)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      完整矩阵揭示清晰的法官二分法。GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 在 ~83% 的 cell 中呈现 Blindspot\n      （BT 显著但 Likert NS），仅 AlpacaEval verbosity（BT 84.1%）例外——极端效应导致 Likert 也检测到（d=0.375）。\n      Claude 和 Llama 的所有 cell 均为 \"both NS\"：它们没有 style bias，\n      因此不存在 Blindspot（Blindspot 前提是 bias 存在但 Likert 检测不到）。\n      Attenuation threshold 约 BT 80%——只有 BT 超过此阈值 Likert 才开始检测。\n      这在 worst 档下 reframe 为：Blindspot 是 biased judge + Likert measurement attenuation 的组合，\n      而非 universal phenomenon。CSD 的诊断价值在于区分 \"has bias but Likert misses it\" vs \"genuinely no bias\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Blindspot Classification Summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Category | GPT-4o | Qwen3-32B | Claude | Llama-70B |\n          |----------|--------|-----------|--------|-----------|\n          | Blindspot (BT sig, Likert NS) | 5 | 6 | 0 | 0 |\n          | Both significant | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n          | Both NS (no bias) | 0 | 0 | 2 | 2 |\n          | Marginal / exploratory | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: BT win rate (x-axis) vs |Likert Cohen's d| (y-axis), each dot = one cell, colored by judge. 显著性分区线在 BT=50% (vertical) 和 d=0.2 (horizontal)。右下象限 = Blindspot zone。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档下 sensitivity matrix 的价值转向：\"CSD diagnoses which judges are susceptible\"\n      替代 \"Likert universally fails\"。7 个 both-NS cells 对审稿人可能显得无信息，\n      需强调 both-NS 在 CSD 下是 positive finding（confirmed absence of bias），\n      而 Likert-only 分析无法区分 \"no bias\" vs \"bias but undetected\"。\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (multi-judge)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Original vs RATE double-rewrite（same style）pairwise 对比，扩展到 4 个法官。\n      量化与 style manipulation 无关的 rewriting artifact preference。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_placebo_bt: 0.597\n      gpt4o_placebo_bt_ci: [0.521, 0.673]\n      gpt4o_placebo_bt_p: 0.018\n      qwen32b_placebo_bt: 0.583\n      qwen32b_placebo_bt_ci: [0.507, 0.659]\n      qwen32b_placebo_bt_p: 0.038\n      claude_placebo_bt: 0.538\n      claude_placebo_bt_ci: [0.462, 0.614]\n      claude_placebo_bt_p: 0.31\n      llama_placebo_bt: 0.525\n      llama_placebo_bt_ci: [0.449, 0.601]\n      llama_placebo_bt_p: 0.52\n      amplification_biased_judges_mean_pp: 9.0\n      amplification_unbiased_judges_mean_pp: 3.15\n    result_rationale: >\n      Placebo BT 揭示了一个意外发现：amplification 本身也是 architecture-dependent。\n      GPT-4o（59.7%, p=.018）和 Qwen3-32B（58.3%, p=.038）对 same-style rewrite 仍显示显著偏好——\n      它们能检测到 rewriting 引入的微观质量提升（更流畅的过渡、更一致的格式、偶尔的措辞优化），\n      这正是 Jeong et al. 2025 (Comparative Trap) 预测的 amplification mechanism。\n      但 Claude（53.8%, p=.31）和 Llama（52.5%, p=.52）的 placebo BT 接近 50% 且 NS——\n      这些法官对 rewriting artifacts 不敏感，或主动抵消了 artifact preference。\n      关键洞察：amplification 不是 pairwise format 的统一特性，而是与 judge architecture 共变。\n      Biased judges 不仅对 style 更敏感，也对 rewriting polish 更敏感——\n      这可能是同一个底层特征（对 surface-level quality cues 的过度权重）。\n      对叙事的影响：不能用单一 placebo correction 修正所有法官，\n      但 per-judge placebo correction 使 corrected BT 的解释更精确。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Placebo BT by Judge (Architecture-Dependent Amplification)\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge | Placebo BT | 95% CI | p | Amplification |\n          |-------|-----------|--------|---|---------------|\n          | GPT-4o | 59.7% | [52.1, 67.3] | .018* | +9.7pp |\n          | Qwen3-32B | 58.3% | [50.7, 65.9] | .038* | +8.3pp |\n          | Claude | 53.8% | [46.2, 61.4] | .31 | +3.8pp (NS) |\n          | Llama-70B | 52.5% | [44.9, 60.1] | .52 | +2.5pp (NS) |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: observed BT / placebo BT / corrected BT for each judge × axis。Biased judges 的 gap (observed − placebo) 明显大于 unbiased judges。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Amplification 的 architecture-dependence 在 worst 档下意外加强了叙事——\n      不仅 style bias 是 judge-specific，连 rewriting artifact sensitivity 也是。\n      这指向共同的底层机制：某些 RLHF 训练使法官对 surface-level cues 过度敏感。\n      但审稿人可能质疑 per-judge correction 的 validity（small n, wide CI on placebo）。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication n=400 (已完成)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Registry 中已完成。Qwen3-32B × LLMBar × formality 从 n=100 扩至 n=400。\n      BT 67.5% [63.7, 71.3] p=0.0001，CI 宽度缩窄 2×。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 400\n      nli_pass: 355\n      bt_p_formal: 0.675\n      bt_ci: [0.637, 0.713]\n      bt_ci_width_pp: 7.6\n      bt_p: 0.0001\n      likert_ate: -0.059\n      likert_p: 0.5999\n      gee_style_or: 2.15\n      gee_orig_or: 4.99\n      blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有真实数据，与 worst 档完全一致。n=400 将 Qwen3-32B formality BT 估计精度翻倍\n      （CI 从 15.4pp → 7.6pp），点估计从 66.5% 微升至 67.5%（+1pp），确认 n=100 结果的稳定性。\n      在 worst 档下此实验为 biased judges 提供最精确的效应量估计。\n      Corrected BT after placebo: 67.5% − 8.3pp = 59.2% [55.4, 63.0]——\n      即使保守修正后 CI 仍不含 50%，formality bias 在 Qwen3-32B 上稳健成立。\n      Llama 不需要 scaled replication（n=100 已显示 NS，更大 n 不会使 NS 变显著 unless true effect > 0）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      为 Qwen3-32B formality 提供锚定估计。Worst 档下 corrected 59.2% 仍显著——\n      formality bias 在 Qwen3-32B 上比 GPT-4o 更稳健（因基线更高）。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B rewriter)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为第三独立 rewriter，在 formality + verbosity 上\n      生成 counterfactuals 并比较 Qwen3-32B judge 的 BT 结果。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_rewriter_formality_nli_pass: 0.85\n      llama_rewriter_formality_bt: 0.641\n      llama_rewriter_formality_bt_ci: [0.563, 0.719]\n      llama_rewriter_formality_bt_p: 0.001\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_nli_pass: 0.82\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt: 0.748\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.670, 0.826]\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt_p: 0.0001\n      vs_qwen32b_rewriter_formality_delta_pp: -2.4\n      vs_qwen32b_rewriter_verbosity_delta_pp: -2.5\n      vs_gpt4o_rewriter_formality_delta_pp: -0.3\n      ci_overlap_all: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      三个独立 rewriter 家族（Qwen3-32B, GPT-4o, Llama-70B）产生的 BT 差异均 <3.8pp 且 CI 完全重叠。\n      Llama rewriter 的 NLI pass rate 略低（82-85% vs 88-90%），因其 instruction following\n      能力稍弱于 Qwen3-32B，偶尔在 style manipulation 时引入更大的内容变化。\n      但通过的 pairs 产生的 BT 与其他 rewriters 一致——说明 bias detection 不依赖特定 rewriter。\n      在 worst 档下此实验是防御性的：即使 Llama judge 不 biased，rewriter independence\n      确保 GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 的 bias 不是 Qwen3-32B rewriter 的 artifact。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Rewriter Independence (Qwen3-32B Judge, LLMBar)\"\n        content: |\n          | Rewriter | Formality BT | Verbosity BT | NLI Pass Rate |\n          |----------|-------------|-------------|--------------|\n          | Qwen3-32B | 66.5% | 77.3% | 88% |\n          | GPT-4o | 64.4% | 73.5% | 90% |\n          | Llama-70B | 64.1% | 74.8% | 83.5% |\n          | Δ max | 2.4pp | 3.8pp | 6.5pp |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT + 95% CI for 3 rewriters, grouped by axis. All CIs overlap substantially.\"\n    analysis: >\n      三 rewriter 一致性排除 rewriter-family artifact。Worst 档下此实验非决定性但必要——\n      确保 biased judges 的信号来自 judge 而非 rewriter。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (已有数据)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o API 对 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs 的评分。\n      Registry 中已完成（gpt4o_verbosity, gpt4o_register）。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt: 0.760\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.688, 0.828]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p: 0.0001\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate: 0.116\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p: 0.403\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_style_or: 10.97\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.44\n      gpt4o_verbosity_blindspot: true\n      gpt4o_register_bt: 0.570\n      gpt4o_register_bt_p: 0.04\n      gpt4o_register_likert_ate: 0.0\n      gpt4o_register_likert_p: 0.785\n      gpt4o_register_gee_style_or: 1.88\n      gpt4o_register_gee_orig_or: 2.21\n      gpt4o_register_blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有真实数据，与 worst 档一致。GPT-4o verbosity BT=76.0% 是全矩阵第二强信号\n      （仅次于 Qwen3-32B verbosity 77.3%），GEE 确认纯 style bias（Style OR=10.97, Orig NS）。\n      Likert ATE=+0.12 p=0.40 确认 Blindspot。\n      Register BT=57.0% 边际显著（p=0.04），GEE 显示 originality 主导（OR=2.21 > style OR=1.88）。\n      在 worst 档下，GPT-4o verbosity 是最稳健的 Blindspot 展示——\n      corrected BT = 76.0% − 10.8pp = 65.2%，仍远高于 50%。\n      GPT-4o formality corrected = 63.0% − 9.7pp = 53.3%，变得 marginal。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      真实数据。Worst 档下 GPT-4o verbosity 是 strongest surviving claim after placebo correction。\n\n  - name: \"Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct third target judge\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.3-70B 作为第三个 target judge（区别于 Claude negative control）。\n      对已有 NLI-filtered formality + verbosity counterfactual pairs 进行\n      pairwise comparison + Likert scoring。核心 worst-tier experiment。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_formality_bt: 0.523\n      llama_formality_bt_ci: [0.448, 0.598]\n      llama_formality_bt_p: 0.52\n      llama_formality_likert_ate: 0.022\n      llama_formality_likert_p: 0.81\n      llama_formality_likert_d: 0.025\n      llama_formality_likert_tie_rate: 0.71\n      llama_formality_consistency_rate: 0.53\n      llama_formality_gee_style_or: 1.15\n      llama_formality_gee_style_p: 0.68\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_or: 2.85\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_p: 0.008\n      llama_verbosity_bt: 0.535\n      llama_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.460, 0.610]\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p: 0.35\n      llama_verbosity_likert_ate: -0.035\n      llama_verbosity_likert_p: 0.72\n      llama_verbosity_likert_d: -0.031\n      llama_verbosity_likert_tie_rate: 0.68\n      llama_verbosity_consistency_rate: 0.55\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_or: 1.28\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_p: 0.48\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.92\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_p: 0.82\n      llama_n_pairs_formality: 88\n      llama_n_pairs_verbosity: 86\n      llama_tost_formality_p: 0.024\n      llama_tost_verbosity_p: 0.018\n      llama_tost_margin: 0.15\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-70B 在两个主要轴上均无显著 style bias，是 worst 档的核心定义特征。\n\n      Formality BT=52.3%（p=0.52）：与 coin flip 无显著差异。GEE 分解显示 style OR=1.15 (p=0.68, NS)\n      但 orig OR=2.85 (p=0.008, sig)——Llama 能检测到 formal→casual rewrite 导致的内容质量变化\n      （originality effect），但完全不受 formality style direction 影响。\n      这与 Claude 的 pattern（BT=56.2%, style OR=1.47, orig OR=6.66）一致但更极端：\n      Llama 的 style sensitivity 接近零，而 Claude 至少有 marginal 倾向。\n\n      Verbosity BT=53.5%（p=0.35）：同样 NS。GEE 中 style OR=1.28 (p=0.48) 和 orig OR=0.92 (p=0.82) \n      均 NS——Llama 对 verbosity manipulation 完全无差别，既不偏好 verbose 也不偏好 concise，\n      且不检测到任何 originality effect（与 formality 不同）。\n      这与 verbosity 的 \"pure style axis\" 特征一致：GEE 中 GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 的 orig OR 也 NS，\n      说明 verbosity manipulation 不改变内容质量——所以对 verbosity 不敏感的法官应 both axes NS。\n\n      架构解释：Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct 使用 Meta 的 RLHF pipeline，\n      其 preference data 主要来源于 human annotators（非 GPT-4 distillation），\n      annotator 指南强调 helpfulness 和 factuality 而非 stylistic polish。\n      GPT-4o 的 RLHF 可能包含对 verbose/formal 输出的隐式偏好（training data 中 verbose answers\n      被人类标注者评为 \"more helpful\"）。Qwen3-32B 的大量 synthetic preference data\n      可能放大了 style-correlated quality signal。\n      Llama 和 Claude 的训练范式避免了这种 style-quality 混淆。\n\n      TOST 在 Δ=0.15 margin 下确认等价性（formality p=0.024, verbosity p=0.018），\n      提供 \"no bias\" 的正向统计证据（vs 仅 \"fail to reject H0\"）。\n      注意 TOST 在 Δ=0.10 下也通过（不同于 Claude 在 Δ=0.10 下未通过），\n      因为 Llama 的 point estimate 更接近 50%（52.3-53.5% vs Claude 54.1-56.2%）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Complete Evidence Matrix (4 Judges × 2 Primary Axes)\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis | GPT-4o BT / Likert p | Qwen3-32B BT / Likert p | Claude BT / Likert p | Llama-70B BT / Likert p |\n          |------|---------------------|------------------------|---------------------|----------------------|\n          | Formality | 63.0%*** / .332 | 66.5%*** / .908 | 56.2%† / .721 | 52.3% / .81 |\n          | Verbosity | 76.0%*** / .403 | 77.3%*** / .179 | 54.1% / .743 | 53.5% / .72 |\n      - title: \"Table: Llama-70B GEE Decomposition\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis | Style OR | Style p | Orig OR | Orig p | Interpretation |\n          |------|---------|---------|---------|--------|----------------|\n          | Formality | 1.15 | .68 | 2.85 | .008** | Originality only |\n          | Verbosity | 1.28 | .48 | 0.92 | .82 | Neither effect |\n      - title: \"Table: TOST Equivalence Results (Δ=0.15)\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge | Formality TOST p | Verbosity TOST p | Equivalence? |\n          |-------|-----------------|-----------------|-------------|\n          | Claude | .155 | .070 | No (underpowered) |\n          | Llama-70B | .024 | .018 | Yes (both axes) |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT win probability + 95% CI for 4 judges × 2 axes, 水平虚线 at 50%。GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 右移显著，Claude/Llama 围绕 50%。\"\n      - \"GEE coefficient plot: Style OR (filled) vs Orig OR (hollow) for 4 judges × 2 axes。Biased judges 的 Style OR >> 1，unbiased judges 的 Style OR ≈ 1。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Llama NS 结果使法官 split 从潜在的 3/4 biased 降为 2/4。\n      叙事核心转向：CSD reveals architecture-dependent susceptibility — not all judges are biased，\n      but CSD can diagnose which are and which aren't。\n      优势：架构特异性 + TOST equivalence = novel empirical finding + methodological rigor。\n      劣势：审稿人可能认为 \"half your judges show no bias\" 降低 practical urgency。\n      防御：precisely BECAUSE bias is judge-specific, per-judge auditing tools like CSD are necessary——\n      users cannot assume their judge is unbiased without testing.\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B focused)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      MF1 最强防御实验。Original vs double-rewrite pairs（same style direction，\n      仅 rewriting artifact 差异）。GPT-4o（API）+ Qwen3-32B（local）。\n      使用 verified_scaled_formality.jsonl 和 verified_verbosity.jsonl 中的 double_rewrite_text。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formality_placebo_bt: 0.597\n      gpt4o_formality_placebo_ci: [0.523, 0.671]\n      gpt4o_formality_placebo_p: 0.015\n      gpt4o_verbosity_placebo_bt: 0.608\n      gpt4o_verbosity_placebo_ci: [0.534, 0.682]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_placebo_p: 0.007\n      qwen32b_formality_placebo_bt: 0.583\n      qwen32b_formality_placebo_ci: [0.509, 0.657]\n      qwen32b_formality_placebo_p: 0.035\n      qwen32b_verbosity_placebo_bt: 0.591\n      qwen32b_verbosity_placebo_ci: [0.517, 0.665]\n      qwen32b_verbosity_placebo_p: 0.021\n      corrected_gpt4o_verbosity: 0.652\n      corrected_gpt4o_formality: 0.533\n      corrected_qwen32b_verbosity: 0.682\n      corrected_qwen32b_formality: 0.582\n      amplification_gpt4o_mean_pp: 10.25\n      amplification_qwen32b_mean_pp: 8.7\n      amplification_cross_axis_delta_gpt4o: 1.1\n      amplification_cross_axis_delta_qwen32b: 0.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Placebo BT 显著 >50% 是 worst 档的第二定义特征（仅次于 Llama NS）。\n\n      GPT-4o placebo: formality 59.7% (p=.015), verbosity 60.8% (p=.007)。\n      Qwen3-32B placebo: formality 58.3% (p=.035), verbosity 59.1% (p=.021)。\n      所有四个 cell 的 placebo BT 均显著 >50%，确认 pairwise format 中存在 rewriting artifact preference。\n\n      机制：LLM double-rewrite 即使保持 style direction 不变，也引入微观改进——\n      更自然的句法连接、更一致的标点格式、偶尔的同义替换使行文更流畅。\n      这些 surface-level improvements 在 pairwise forced comparison 中被检测到。\n      Critically，amplification 在同一法官内跨轴近似均匀：\n      GPT-4o formality 9.7pp vs verbosity 10.8pp (Δ=1.1pp)，\n      Qwen3-32B formality 8.3pp vs verbosity 9.1pp (Δ=0.8pp)。\n      这支持 \"amplification is a judge-level constant, style bias is the differential signal\" 论点。\n\n      Corrected BT（observed − amplification）：\n      - Verbosity: GPT-4o 65.2%, Qwen3-32B 68.2% → 仍远 >50%，强效应\n      - Formality: GPT-4o 53.3%, Qwen3-32B 58.2% → GPT-4o marginal, Qwen3-32B moderate\n\n      GPT-4o formality corrected 53.3% 是 worst 档的关键弱点：\n      bootstrapped corrected CI 可能为 [46.8, 59.8]，包含 50%——\n      GPT-4o formality 在保守修正后可能不再显著。\n      但 Qwen3-32B formality corrected 58.2% 更稳健（CI ~[51.5, 64.9]）。\n      Per-axis claim stratification 在 worst 档下进一步分层：\n      verbosity = \"robust after correction\"，formality = \"judge-dependent after correction\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Placebo BT and Corrected Style Effect\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge | Axis | Observed BT | Placebo BT | Corrected BT | Status |\n          |-------|------|-----------|-----------|-------------|--------|\n          | GPT-4o | Verbosity | 76.0%*** | 60.8%** | 65.2% | Strong |\n          | GPT-4o | Formality | 63.0%*** | 59.7%* | 53.3% | Marginal |\n          | Qwen3-32B | Verbosity | 77.3%*** | 59.1%* | 68.2% | Strong |\n          | Qwen3-32B | Formality | 66.5%*** | 58.3%* | 58.2% | Moderate |\n      - title: \"Table: Amplification Uniformity Within Judge\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge | Formality Amp. | Verbosity Amp. | Cross-Axis Δ |\n          |-------|---------------|---------------|-------------|\n          | GPT-4o | 9.7pp | 10.8pp | 1.1pp |\n          | Qwen3-32B | 8.3pp | 9.1pp | 0.8pp |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar: observed BT = 50% baseline + amplification floor + corrected style signal, for each judge×axis cell。\"\n      - \"Line plot: amplification pp (y) vs axis (x) for two judges, showing near-parallel lines confirming uniformity.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Placebo >50% 迫使论文增加 \"amplification accounting\" 章节（~0.5 page）。\n      Worst 档下 formality claim 被削弱但 verbosity claim 稳健。\n      关键防御 narrative：\n      (1) Amplification 跨轴均匀（Δ < 1.1pp）→ 轴间差异不是 amplification 造成的\n      (2) Claude/Llama placebo ≈ 50% → amplification 是 judge-specific，不是 format-universal\n      (3) Corrected BT 是 conservative lower bound（assumes ALL amplification is artifact）\n      审稿人路径：honest + conservative correction → methodological credibility，\n      即使 formality GPT-4o cell 失去 significance。\n\n  - name: \"NLI gate ablation (pass vs fail BT)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: >\n      Bounding analysis：计算 NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs 的 BT，\n      量化 NLI gate 对 bias signal 的影响。Verbosity + formality 两轴，Qwen3-32B judge。\n    expected_results:\n      formality_nli_pass_n: 88\n      formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.665\n      formality_nli_fail_n: 12\n      formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.652\n      formality_pass_minus_fail_pp: 1.3\n      formality_fail_bt_ci: [0.38, 0.92]\n      formality_all_bt: 0.653\n      verbosity_nli_pass_n: 86\n      verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_nli_fail_n: 14\n      verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.748\n      verbosity_pass_minus_fail_pp: 2.5\n      verbosity_fail_bt_ci: [0.50, 0.99]\n      verbosity_all_bt: 0.765\n    result_rationale: >\n      NLI-fail 组极小（formality n=12, verbosity n=14），CI 宽达 40-50pp，完全无统计区分力。\n\n      Formality: NLI-pass BT=66.5% vs NLI-fail BT=65.2%, Δ=+1.3pp。\n      方向符合预期（NLI gate 移除了 content-contaminated pairs 后信号略纯），\n      但 fail 组 CI [38%, 92%] 与 pass 组估计完全重叠——差异不可区分于噪声。\n      All-pairs BT=65.3%（vs NLI-pass 66.5%, Δ=−1.2pp）——NLI gate 几乎不改变估计。\n\n      Verbosity: NLI-pass BT=77.3% vs NLI-fail BT=74.8%, Δ=+2.5pp。\n      同样方向正确但 fail 组 CI [50%, 99%] 无信息量。\n      All-pairs BT=76.5%（vs NLI-pass 77.3%, Δ=−0.8pp）。\n\n      Inconclusive 的原因：NLI-fail pairs 本身是异质的——\n      有些是 content genuinely changed（应被排除），有些是 NLI model 误判（仍有效）。\n      n=12-14 无法区分这些子群。\n      \n      在 worst 档下，这意味着无法用 NLI ablation 论证 \"NLI gate removes content-mediated signal\"——\n      gate 的 added value 在统计上不可证。但可以说 \"NLI gate does not inflate BT\"\n      （all-pairs BT 与 pass-only BT 差异 <2pp），which is a necessary condition for the gate\n      not being a signal-amplifier.\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: NLI Gate Ablation — BT by Subset\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis | NLI-pass BT (n) | NLI-fail BT (n) | All BT (n) | Δ pass−fail | Δ pass−all |\n          |------|----------------|----------------|-----------|------------|-----------|\n          | Formality | 66.5% (88) | 65.2% (12) | 65.3% (100) | +1.3pp | +1.2pp |\n          | Verbosity | 77.3% (86) | 74.8% (14) | 76.5% (100) | +2.5pp | +0.8pp |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT + 95% CI for pass/fail/all subsets, by axis. Fail group CI bars span nearly full [0, 1] range.\"\n    analysis: >\n      NLI ablation 是 worst 档下 weakest experiment。论文中用 1-2 句报告：\n      \"BT estimates are stable with or without NLI filtering (Δ < 2.5pp), \n      suggesting the gate is conservative rather than signal-amplifying. \n      However, the NLI-fail subgroup is too small (n=12-14) to quantify \n      content-mediated signal directly.\"\n      不作为 anti-amplification 主线论据。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      定性 anti-amplification 论证：3 轴的 NLI rejection rate（manipulation invasiveness proxy）\n      vs observed BT vs corrected BT 梯度分析。仅 3 个数据点，qualitative not statistical。\n    expected_results:\n      verbosity_nli_rejection_rate: 0.14\n      verbosity_observed_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_corrected_bt: 0.682\n      verbosity_gee_style_or: 13.10\n      formality_nli_rejection_rate: 0.112\n      formality_observed_bt: 0.665\n      formality_corrected_bt: 0.582\n      formality_gee_style_or: 4.20\n      register_nli_rejection_rate: 0.06\n      register_observed_bt: 0.553\n      register_corrected_bt: 0.470\n      register_gee_style_or: 1.91\n      gradient_monotonic_observed: true\n      gradient_monotonic_corrected: true\n      register_corrected_below_50: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      三轴梯度在 worst 档下保持单调但被 placebo correction 部分削弱。\n\n      Observed gradient（Qwen3-32B, LLMBar）：\n      verbosity 77.3% > formality 66.5% > register 55.3%\n      NLI rejection: verbosity 14% > formality 11.2% > register 6%\n      单调关系：更 invasive 的 manipulation → 更高的 BT。\n\n      Anti-amplification argument: 如果 pairwise format 统一放大所有 style differences，\n      则所有轴的 BT 应相似（或仅与 manipulation magnitude 成比例，不与 axis identity 相关）。\n      22pp 的跨轴变异（55-77%）远大于 amplification 的跨轴变异（<1pp within judge）\n      → per-axis style bias 是主要 driver，不是 uniform format amplification。\n\n      Corrected gradient: verbosity 68.2% > formality 58.2% > register ~47%。\n      Register corrected BT 低于 50%——解释为 originality effect 在 correction 后\n      完全掩盖了 marginal style signal（register GEE: orig OR=5.72 >> style OR=1.91）。\n      这并不矛盾：register 的 style manipulation 很轻（NLI rejection 仅 6%），\n      实际 style bias 可能确实很弱或不存在。\n\n      但 worst 档下的反论：maybe more invasive manipulation 不仅暴露更多 bias，\n      也 CREATES 更多 artifact（因为改动更大）。3 个点无法排除这种混淆。\n      这是一个 qualitative argument 的固有局限。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-Axis Gradient (Qwen3-32B, LLMBar)\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis | NLI Reject % | Observed BT | Amplification | Corrected BT | GEE Style OR |\n          |------|-------------|------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|\n          | Verbosity | 14.0% | 77.3% | 9.1pp | 68.2% | 13.10*** |\n          | Formality | 11.2% | 66.5% | 8.3pp | 58.2% | 4.20*** |\n          | Register | 6.0% | 55.3% | ~8.5pp* | ~46.8% | 1.91* |\n          * Register placebo estimated from judge-level average\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-variable line plot: NLI rejection % (x-axis), observed BT (left y-axis, solid), corrected BT (left y-axis, dashed), GEE Style OR (right y-axis, dotted). All three monotonically decrease left-to-right.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-axis gradient 在 worst 档下是 anti-amplification 论证的 best available argument\n      （NLI ablation inconclusive, placebo >50%）。虽然仅 3 点且无法 statistically test，\n      定性 monotonicity + amplification uniformity 的组合提供 reasonable evidence：\n      \"CSD detects axis-specific style bias, not uniform format artifact.\"\n      Register corrected BT <50% 诚实报告——进一步区分了 3 axes 的 claim strength：\n      verbosity (strong) >> formality (moderate) >> register (not surviving correction)。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"510a4aa3-9bfc-4c61-ab4d-d3e433e97f95","total_cost_usd":1.5882324999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":66250,"cache_read_input_tokens":326514,"output_tokens":39436,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":66250,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":13505,"cache_read_input_tokens":69920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7777,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7777},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":24888,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.024978,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":39436,"cacheReadInputTokens":326514,"cacheCreationInputTokens":66250,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.5632544999999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"21dba93a-3bb7-4552-9d8f-bf12e38d682e"}
